                        "entry_id": "6fbc325a-01d3-3239-b89d-28896a21ba8a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Restive, resistant to control."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British",
                            "regional"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e082e286-9be5-43c1-9bc8-322e7a9fdfcc",
                                "sense_id": "f9c70eec-4737-301a-8834-be7a6daf13a6",
                                "text": "In vaine the Pagan bannes, and sweares, and rayles, / And backe with both his hands unto him hayles / The resty raynes […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84ba675d-10fb-4642-9d73-272e37fba8ed",
                                "sense_id": "f9c70eec-4737-301a-8834-be7a6daf13a6",
                                "text": "[N]either knovv I vvhether it is more hard to manage of the tvvo, a dejected eſtate, or a proſperous, vvhether vve may be more incommodated vvith a reſty horſe, or vvith a tyred one: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51101286-284b-4ba2-a527-35dead6ab868",
                                "sense_id": "f9c70eec-4737-301a-8834-be7a6daf13a6",
                                "text": "I could not come a moment sooner; I hardly expected to get here at all, for my horse has been so confounded resty I could not tell how to get him along."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84979827-1571-4dc1-a48b-aa1308aad4cd",
                                "sense_id": "f9c70eec-4737-301a-8834-be7a6daf13a6",
                                "text": "“Catch hold of the pack-beasts!” I shouted, as they shied back upon us, and two were caught and held fast—I know not by whom. The third, the resty one, springing backwards past me, almost on his haunches, jerked his halter wide of my clutch, and in a moment was galloping full flight down the slope."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "676245ad-5d44-37ef-acbf-a5df6e26522e",
                        "entry_id": "6fbc325a-01d3-3239-b89d-28896a21ba8a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Disposed to rest; inactive, lazy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British",
                            "regional"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0503b16-152e-47f2-aed2-41b9e3201b4c",
                                "sense_id": "676245ad-5d44-37ef-acbf-a5df6e26522e",
                                "text": "[…] Come; our stomachs / Will make what’s homely savoury: weariness / Can snore upon the flint, when resty sloth / Finds the down pillow hard."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07036029-26cb-4532-adc4-026c610067b1",
                                "sense_id": "676245ad-5d44-37ef-acbf-a5df6e26522e",
                                "text": "[A]ll [beef] is rejected and unfit for such as lead a resty life, anyways inclined to melancholy, or dry of complexion […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5335446-9470-43f3-89e1-20845703ed72",
                                "sense_id": "676245ad-5d44-37ef-acbf-a5df6e26522e",
                                "text": "[W]hat are Chaplains? In State perhaps they may be listed among the upper Servingmen of som great houshold, and be admitted to som such place, as may stile them the Sewers, or the Yeomen-Ushers of Devotion, where the Maister is too restie, or too rich to say his own prayers, or to bless his own Table."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
